*This strategy is still usable with a Lv. 30 Awakened Bahamut Cat, though it will leave little room for error.
*The Research Cat Combos can be replaced with Unit Attack Up Combos.
}}

'''Battle:''' At the beginning, continuously spam meatshields and Courier Cat to kill of the Those Guys for cash. When Queen Mother V spawns, start spamming Octopus Cats, Fishman Cats, and Bullet Train Cats as well (in that order of priority; Courier is always first priority). The goal is to juggle the Rain D. with your courier stack so he can't attack, all while doing high amounts of damage to Queen Mother V with your rushers. When Haniwanwan spawns, send in Awakened Bahamut Cat; if performed correctly, Bahamut should kill Haniwanwan while taking no damage at all. After Haniwanwan dies, you can stop spawning Octopus Cats if you wish, but you will more than likely have enough money to continue to do so. Queen Mother V should die quickly, after which you are free to tear apart the base.

If you can't destroy the base before Slepnir spawns, '''DO NOT ESCAPE!''' There is still a very high chance that you'll be able to finish the level. Rain D. will die around this timeframe, and combined with Queen Mother V's money drop, you'll be able to endlessly spam the non-combo units to throw at Slepnir. Wait until H. Nah spawns, then deploy your second Bahamut; time your Thunderbolt Cannon so that it hits the targets right before Bahamut reaches them. At Lv.40, Bahamut should get two hits and knock back Slepnir. The rest is just a matter of endurance, with Gabriels arriving occasionally to provide you with money (Note that they are limited, however). When the second Rain D. arrives, use Slepnir as a stepping stone for Courier to snipe it and knock it back. H. Nah and Slepnir should die at around the same time, after which is battle is basically won.

